---
layout: layouts/product.njk
permalink: /phone/applications/desktop/macos/
title: "VoiceTel Phone for macOS — Install Guide & FAQ"
description: "Download, install, and troubleshoot VoiceTel Phone and VoiceML Phone on macOS (.dmg / .zip) for Apple Silicon and Intel Macs. Signed and notarized builds, SHA-256 checksums, and FAQ."
platform: macos
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}
{%- set voicetel = phoneApps.apps | where("key", "voicetel") | first %}
{%- set macArm = voicetel.desktop | where("platform", "macos") | where("format", ".dmg") | where("arch", "arm64") | first %}
{%- set macIntel = voicetel.desktop | where("platform", "macos") | where("format", ".dmg") | where("arch", "x86-64") | first %}

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Desktop &middot; macOS</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">VoiceTel Phone for macOS.</h1>
			<p class="lede">Download, install, and troubleshoot the macOS app (.dmg or .zip) on Apple Silicon and Intel Macs. VoiceML Phone, the same softphone for VoiceML accounts, is listed alongside.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="#download">Download for macOS {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/phone/applications/desktop/">All desktop clients</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set kpis = [
				{ label: "Version", value: voicetel.version, sub: "Built " ~ voicetel.built },
				{ label: "Apple Silicon", value: macArm.size, sub: ".dmg · arm64 · M1–M4" },
				{ label: "Intel", value: macIntel.size, sub: ".dmg · x86-64 · also runs on Apple Silicon via Rosetta 2" },
				{ label: "Gatekeeper", value: "Notarized", sub: "Signed and notarized by Apple; opens without warnings" }
			] %}
			{% include "partials/v2/kpi-grid.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="download" aria-labelledby="download-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">1 &middot; Download</p>
			<h2 id="download-heading">Choose the build that matches your Mac.</h2>
			<p class="lede"><strong>arm64</strong> for Apple Silicon (M1&ndash;M4), <strong>x86-64</strong> for Intel; the Intel build also runs on Apple Silicon via Rosetta 2. If unsure, use the <strong>.dmg</strong>; the .zip is the same app as an archive for scripted installs. All macOS builds are signed and notarized by Apple, so Gatekeeper opens them without warnings.</p>
		</div>
		{%- for app in phoneApps.apps %}
		{%- set files = app.desktop | where("platform", platform) %}
		<h3 class="subsection-heading" id="download-{{ app.key }}">{{ app.name }} {{ app.version }}</h3>
		<div class="prose"><p>{{ app.audience }}</p></div>
		<div class="table-container">
			<table class="data-table">
				<thead>
					<tr><th scope="col">Build</th><th scope="col">SHA-256</th></tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{%- for file in files %}
					<tr>
						<td>{{ file.format }} &middot; {{ file.arch }}<br><a href="{{ phoneApps.baseUrl }}{{ file.file }}">{{ file.file }}</a> &middot; {{ file.size }}</td>
						<td><code class="mono">{{ file.sha256 | replace(r/^(.{32})/, "$1<wbr>") | safe }}</code></td>
					</tr>
					{%- endfor %}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		{%- endfor %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="verify" aria-labelledby="verify-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">2 &middot; Verify checksum</p>
				<h2 id="verify-heading">Compare the SHA-256 before you install.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Optional: validate file integrity by comparing SHA-256 checksums. Open Terminal, run the command against the file you downloaded, and compare the output with the value listed above.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set code %}{% highlight "bash" %}shasum -a 256 VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}-arm64.dmg
# substitute whichever file you downloaded;
# the output must match the checksum listed above{% endhighlight %}{% endset %}
				{%- set terminal = { label: "Terminal", pill: "SHA-256", code: code } %}
				{% include "partials/v2/terminal.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row row--reverse">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">3 &middot; Install and first launch</p>
				<h2 id="install-heading">Drag to Applications, allow the microphone, sign in.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Open the disk image and drag the app to Applications, or unzip the archive for scripted installs. On first launch, allow microphone access and enter the credentials for your account.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual" id="firstlaunch">
				{%- set steps = [
					{ title: "Open the .dmg", body: "Open the downloaded <strong>.dmg</strong>." },
					{ title: "Drag to Applications", body: "Drag <strong>VoiceTel</strong> (or <strong>VoiceML</strong>) to the <strong>Applications</strong> folder. Eject the disk image when finished." },
					{ title: "Scripted installs", body: "Unzip the <strong>.zip</strong> instead and move <code>VoiceTel.app</code> (or <code>VoiceML.app</code>) to Applications." },
					{ title: "Open the app", body: "Open <strong>VoiceTel</strong> from Applications." },
					{ title: "Allow microphone access", body: "Allow access when prompted. If you missed the prompt, go to <em>System Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security &rarr; Microphone</em> and enable access for the app." },
					{ title: "Sign in", body: "Enter your VoiceTel SIP credentials (username, password, display name) as provisioned in the customer portal. In VoiceML Phone, enter your VoiceML activation code under <em>Settings &rarr; Auto Provision</em> instead." }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/step-list.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
			<h2 id="faq-heading">Questions about VoiceTel Phone on macOS.</h2>
		</div>
		{%- set faqs = [
			{ q: "How do I uninstall VoiceTel Phone?", a: "Quit the app, open <em>Applications</em>, and drag <strong>VoiceTel.app</strong> (or <strong>VoiceML.app</strong>) to the Trash." },
			{ q: "The app won’t open after installation", a: "The builds are notarized, so Gatekeeper should open them directly. If your Mac’s security policy still blocks the app, right-click it and choose <em>Open</em>, or go to <em>System Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security</em> and click <em>Open Anyway</em>." },
			{ q: "The microphone isn’t working", a: "Ensure the app has permission under <em>System Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security &rarr; Microphone</em>. Also check <em>System Settings &rarr; Sound</em> for the correct input device." },
			{ q: "Can I pre-configure the app for my users?", a: "Yes. Place <code>voicetel.json</code> under <code>~/Library/Application Support/VoiceTelPhone/</code> for user-level deployment, or <code>/Library/Application Support/VoiceTelPhone/</code> for system-wide deployment." },
			{ q: "Upgrading from an earlier version?", a: "Fully quit the running app from the menu-bar icon (right-click &rarr; <em>Quit</em>) before installing; otherwise the single-instance lock re-focuses the old version." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/faq.njk" %}

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Need credentials first?</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Sign up to provision SIP credentials, then install VoiceTel Phone on every Mac that needs to make calls.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signup/">Free trial {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/phone/applications/desktop/">All desktop clients</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
